Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Payoffs and dynamics in bimorphic populations", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.939807201726128*^9, 3.9398072092363997`*^9}, {
  3.968576986093499*^9, 
  3.9685770386007633`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9c3381b5-674f-4efe-ae3e-\
93d5b51fcfad"],

Cell["\<\
This Manipulate shows the expected payoff of each strategy in bimorphic \
populations, together with the (1-dimensional) mean dynamic at the bottom of \
the plot: arrows
point in the direction of movement and circles indicate the location of rest \
points. 

Errors are modeled as unintended action flips in the stage game, with \
probability \[Epsilon]. Parameter \[Delta] is the continuation probability of \
a partnership in which both players decide to stay. Experimentation (with \
probability \[Mu]) consists in choosing one of the two strategies at random. 

Note that errors affect the expected payoff obtained by each strategy, but \
experimentation does not. Experimentation affects the dynamics, including the \
existence and location of rest points.
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9688087027578297`*^9, 3.9688087247053003`*^9}, 
   3.968809007712736*^9, {3.968809048843854*^9, 3.968809164626637*^9}, {
   3.968809255186688*^9, 3.968809314364915*^9}, {3.968809350361679*^9, 
   3.968809381672908*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4551b46e-2323-49fd-b026-\
0d75fec47e8a"],

